      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When addressing past results, focus on the learning experience and subsequent improvements. For instance, mention the 5% increase in coral health as a concrete starting point, emphasizing lessons learned and the strengths utilized from that project, such as experienced team or logistical efficiencies. Reflect on the iterative process of research and adaptation, and how these insights directly inform the strategies and aspirations of the new project. Transparently but constructively presenting your history lends credibility and demonstrates commitment to impact. Highlight proactive steps taken to achieve the 20% target and position the new proposal as a significant leap forward, fueled by validated experience.",
